[
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Lab 3: real weather from a web API\n\n**Goal:** fetch the real weather for your site.\n\n**You will build:**\n1. `CampusWeather`, a Connector: when anything is published to `campus/weather/request`, it calls [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com) and publishes the answer to `campus/weather/raw`. ProcessWeather (Lab 2) takes it from there.\n2. `RequestWeather`, an Action: publishes `poll` to `campus/weather/request` every 5 minutes.\n\nA Connector links the broker to the outside world. Community Edition allows 3; the lesson uses exactly 3 (this one and two in Lab 4)."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 1. CampusWeather\n\nThe broker fills in `{env.WEATHER_LAT}` and `{env.WEATHER_LON}` from the variables you set in `00-setup`. To change a Connector later, edit the cell and run it again: the new version replaces the old one. (`DEFINE ROUTE` is the older spelling of `DEFINE CONNECTOR`; both work.)"
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE CONNECTOR CampusWeather WITH TYPE REST_API\n    ADD REST_API_CONFIG\n        WITH BASE_ADDRESS \"https://api.open-meteo.com\"\n        WITH ENABLE_CLIENT \"true\"\n        WITH USE_SSL \"true\"\n    ADD EVENT GetCurrentWeather\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\"\n        WITH METHOD \"GET\"\n        WITH ENDPOINT \"/v1/forecast?latitude={env.WEATHER_LAT}&longitude={env.WEATHER_LON}&current=temperature_2m,wind_speed_10m&wind_speed_unit=kmh\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 2. RequestWeather\n\nThe payload does not matter: the Connector reads the site from the variables."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE ACTION RequestWeather\nON EVERY 5 MINUTES DO\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\" WITH \"poll\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check it worked\n\n**Don't wait for RequestWeather:** its first poll comes 5 minutes after you deploy it. In **Data Viewer → Publish**, publish `poll` to `campus/weather/request` yourself.\n\nWithin a few seconds: the Open-Meteo answer on `campus/weather/raw`, then a reading for your site on `campus/weather/reading`.\n\nSomething on `campus/weather/errors` instead? Read it. *\"The service is overloaded\"* means Open-Meteo is busy: wait a minute and poll again.\n\nDocs: [REST API connectors](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/routes/rest-api-routes)."
 }
]
